WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:04.396
This briefing comes from Book 14 of
the Federal Modernization Workbook,

2
00:00:04.396 --> 00:00:06.787
Federal Compliance and Authorization.

3
00:00:06.787 --> 00:00:09.612
It's written for authorizing officials,

4
00:00:09.612 --> 00:00:13.037
information system security
officers and C I Os.

5
00:00:13.037 --> 00:00:17.558
I'll take four questions: why every
control needs proof rather than a promise,

6
00:00:17.558 --> 00:00:20.931
and what the federal clock now
asks for; what the baseline,

7
00:00:20.931 --> 00:00:24.735
the closure rule and the agency-level
control families require;

8
00:00:24.735 --> 00:00:29.687
who owns compliance; and how to build the
authorization package and keep it current.

9
00:00:29.687 --> 00:00:32.483
The short version: a control
is closed when the thing

10
00:00:32.483 --> 00:00:35.538
that closes it is running and
the record shows it working.

11
00:00:35.538 --> 00:00:38.880
Everything else is a
promise, and promises age.
